{"path":"ranges/common_range","title":"std::ranges::common_range","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::ranges::</span>common_range","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/ranges/common_range","section":"ranges","kind":"page","summary":"The common_range concept is a refinement of range for which std::ranges::begin() and std::ranges::end() return the same type (e.g. all standard library containers).","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/ranges\">&lt;ranges&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>concept common_range <span class=\"sy1\">=</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/range\"><span class=\"kw2916\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">range</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/concepts/same_as\"><span class=\"kw2950\">std::<span class=\"me2\">same_as</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/iterator_t\"><span class=\"kw2908\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">iterator_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/iterator_t\"><span class=\"kw2909\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">sentinel_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The <code>common_range</code> concept is a refinement of <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/range\"><code>range</code></a> for which <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/begin\">std::ranges::begin()</a></span> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/end\">std::ranges::end()</a></span> return the same type (e.g. all standard library containers).\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;ranges&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> A\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">char</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> begin<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">char</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> end<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\nstatic_assert<span class=\"br0\">(</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">ranges</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">common_range</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>A<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> B\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">char</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> begin<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> end<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>  <span class=\"co1\">// not a common_range: begin/end have different types</span>\nstatic_assert<span class=\"br0\">(</span> not std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">ranges</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">common_range</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>B<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> C\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">char</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> begin<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>  <span class=\"co1\">// not a common_range, not even a range: has no end()</span>\nstatic_assert<span class=\"br0\">(</span> not std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">ranges</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">common_range</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>C<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/common_view\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>ranges::common_view</span><span>views::common</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td> converts a <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/view\"><code>view</code></a> into a <strong class=\"selflink\"><code>common_range</code></strong><br><span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> <span class=\"t-mark\">(range adaptor object)</span></td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"ranges","title":"Ranges library (since C++20)"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::ranges::common_range","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++20. The common_range concept is a refinement of range for which std::ranges::begin() and std::ranges::end() return the…"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"ranges::common_view, views::common","note":"con